  "source_wide_identity_guards": [
    "Edible fungi must be edible identified species with suitable condition and flavour; actual species/strain and supplier documentation absent.",
    "General stalk-count limit applies unless product all caps or an added-stalk label disclosure exemption applies; mixed species require appropriate labelling.",
    "Different processing classes change salt, moisture, impurities, microbial hazards and packaging requirements; no favourable-style threshold inheritance.",
    "2.3.62 label has process term and, for stated styles, common+scientific species names, mixed if multiple species, processing-history declaration for nonfresh input, salted-input declaration and added-stalk declaration where relevant.",
    "The old Packaging and Labelling Regulations 2011 referenced in the compendium do not negate current applicable 2020 labelling/other effective legal changes.",
    "Possible permitted ingredients include animal fats, butter, milk and cream; mushrooms/fungi label does NOT imply vegan or milk-allergen-free.",
    "Fungi oil-packs and hermetic/sterilized products require independent documented microbial safety/thermal validation; compendium quality limits do not suffice.",
    "Fungi extract 7% vs concentrate 24% saltless extract and fungi dried concentrate moisture 9% are different distinct specifications.",
    "Mineral impurities are defined as residues after ashing insoluble in HCl; 'none' is source wording, not fabricated numeric LOQ.",
    "No actual finished food CTR metal/mycotoxin/pesticide/microbiology additive full matrix or current-law adjudication exists in this audit; original 137 remain open."
  ],
